  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of a pile of pastel cartoon dragons with horns, bat wings and smiling faces against a pale blue and green ground, signed CRUMP 11.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on wood, signed CRUMP 11 at lower right. Nine rounded dragon creatures in yellow, blue, pink, teal, orange and lilac pile together in the centre: each has a round body, a small horn, a white eye, a smiling mouth, a row of white teeth along a tail or wing edge, and purple or pink bat wings. The ground is a soft pale blue fading to pale green with visible brush strokes. Thick black outlines over flat colour.",
    "impression": "A family photo of baby dragons, all crowding to be in frame. They are more plush toy than monster, and the pale ground makes them look like they are floating in a nursery. The sweetest of the group portraits.",
